plar  across Canada but they also should be  looking at that action plan for the rest  of the province of BC red dresses have  become a symbol for action and awareness  according to Stouts Canada nearly 1 in  10 victims of a violent crime in 2019  were indigenous women whose homicide  rate is six times higher than that of  non-indigenous people each woman  deserved their own cover story a Toronto  non-profit created this newspaper  featuring four thousand cover stories  honoring their lives we also wanted to  define the magnitude in the physical  paper itself the paper weighs about 25  pounds and that really demonstrates that  if you capture the true story of each  indigenous woman who has been missing or  murdered you would see the heaviness of  it it was delivered to the prime  minister's office in the fall calls to  urgently act on recommendations from the  2019 inquiry into missing and murdered  indigenous women and girls have remained  unanswered those calls include appeals  to create a national indigenous and  human rights ombuds person and a  tribunal I hate to say it and I didn't  want to go there but you know if it  wasn't indigenous women with this uh  with would this already be happening you  know because it's indigenous women is  and girls into spirit and gender diverse  is is this why it's taking so long a  spokesperson for the crown indigenous  relations Ministry told Global News in a  written statement it's committed to  accelerating efforts to implement the  national action plan the federal pathway  and the calls to Justice and that in  January a national Roundtable is being  convened by the federal government and  there will be an update on the calls for  an ombuds person and a tribunal the feds  also say they're providing funding to  the assembly of Manitoba Chiefs for a  feasibility study of the Winnipeg  landfills  some also want to see accountability  from the Catholic Church which ran many  of Canada's residential institutions the  issue was ta